/*
  ReferenceLinksSection.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0007 · ReferenceLinksSection (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `ReferenceLinksSection` resolves (table "ReferenceLinksSection") lives here with
  its web `t(key, default)` value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact set of title keys the web source passes to
  `t(link.title)` (features/admin/components/devtools/ReferenceLinksSection.tsx via
  the `REFERENCE_LINKS` constant). These keys are absent from the web en catalog, so
  the web renders the raw key text; the native fallbacks here humanise each key from
  its destination, matching the sibling `ClientUtilitiesSection` precedent. The
  remaining keys back the native-only chrome (the freshness chip + banner, the
  loading / empty / error copy, and accessibility), so the Swift sources hold no
  English literals.
*/

